# These tests pass locally but fail on CI
-AntiVirusMetricsProviderTest.GetMetricsFullName/*
-FileSystemAccessUIHelpersTest.GetElidedPathForDisplayAsTitle
-NotificationHelperLaunchesChrome.ChromeLaunchTest
-PerformanceManagerMetricsProviderDesktopTest.TestCpuThrottlingMetricRecordedWhereAvailable

# This test is disabled because our CIs use Windows Server which doesn't appear
# to have FOLDERID_OneDrive entry in the registry making this test fail.
-PathServiceTest.Get

# These fail due to CHECK in ResourceBundle::GetLocalizedStringImpl because: "If
# this happens in a browser test running on Windows, it may be that dead-code
# elimination stripped out the code that uses the resource, causing the resource
# to be stripped out because the resource is not used by chrome.dll"
-DesktopMediaPickerViewsSingleTabPaneTest.AccessibleProperties

# Upstream flake: 1.0% flake rate over 30 days per LUCI Analysis (182K verdicts).
# FindNewCheckTime() can schedule past Now()+interval due to timezone-dependent
# LocalMidnight() boundary. Already filtered on Linux.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/54960
-PasswordStatusCheckServiceBaseTest.PrefInitialized

# Upstream flake introduced by Chromium commit 56d90776362b5 ("Implement
# platform-agnostic system media permission caching", 2026-07-23), which removed
# the cached IAppCapability COM objects that SystemMediaSourceWin used to hold
# and replaced them with a fresh live query (CreateAppCapability + CheckAccess)
# on every call. The test asserts that two consecutive SystemPermissionStatus()
# calls on the same object return equal values, but nothing caches the result
# anymore, so on CI bots the live WinRT AppCapability check can return a
# different AppCapabilityAccessStatus between the two calls. 0% flaky before
# 2026-07-24, ~0.26% since, per LUCI Analysis (60-day lookback) -- confirms this
# is an upstream regression, not a Brave-specific issue (no chromium_src
# overrides or patches touch this file).
-SystemMediaSourceWinTest.ConstructionDoesNotCrash

